pa-types
========

Origin
------
This crate is a modified fork of the `pa-types` crate from
PrimeIntellect-ai/prime-agent (https://github.com/PrimeIntellect-ai/prime-agent),
the Rust side of the Prime Agent product. It is a serde port of that product's
TypeScript shared vocabulary (TS `packages/ai/src/types.ts` and the wire/domain
contracts under `src/`).

Upstream license: MIT. The upstream license text is vendored at
`vendor/LICENSE-prime-agent`; it also credits the original TypeScript product,
"a port of the Prime Agent TypeScript product, originally Copyright (c) 2025
Mario Zechner". That MIT license and copyright notice apply to this crate.

Modifications by oh-my-tau
--------------------------
This copy has been changed. It is NOT byte-identical to upstream, and files
carrying the upstream header are not verbatim upstream content. Substantive
changes:

* Incident classifier regexes (src/incident/patterns.rs, plus classify/parse/
  anomaly): the log-message patterns are the TypeScript regexes from the TS
  product's `src/cli/incident.ts`, re-expressed with the Rust `regex` crate and
  kept 1:1 with their TypeScript sources so classification semantics match.
  `regex` was added to Cargo.toml for this purpose only.
* Session types (src/session.rs): the session JSONL entry schema, extended and
  adjusted to carry this repo's session records while preserving lossless
  round-trips (unknown fields survive via `#[serde(flatten)] rest: JsonMap`).
* Compat types (src/ai/compat.rs, with ai/mod.rs, routing.rs, thinking_levels.rs):
  the model-compat family (OpenAI-completions compat block, format enums,
  OpenAI-responses and Anthropic compat blocks, `ModelCompat`/`CompatKind`),
  adapted for the models this repo targets.
* Platform contracts (src/platform/): AF_UNIX transport, process identity,
  socket identity, home-dir resolution, and the suspend-to-background signal
  control, including cfg-gated Windows named-pipe support. These carry
  legitimate `unsafe` blocks, so this crate keeps its own `[lints.clippy]`
  table in Cargo.toml instead of inheriting the workspace's
  `unsafe_code = "forbid"`.
* Other touched areas: goal, memory_release, skill_blocks, slash_commands,
  themes, usage, daemon (framing, plane, command, outbound, worker,
  update_flow).

